Z||000003||Pontiaddict||08-02-2001||10:22 PM||||You should be able to get one from a local parts store. If the rod bearing is bad, look for crank damage. You might be better off just finding another motor.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Scott||08-03-2001||03:04 AM||||I don't know much about 2.5 performance, but I've worked with other engines a few times and came to these conclusions.  <BR>A HO cam is a fastest, easiest way to get more power.  If that has been done, add headers and a free-flowing exhaust.  Followed by a HO intake and carb./injection.  Then, ported heads can give alot more power.  And finally, if you more power than these mods can give, increase the displacement .<BR>With a Duke, not many mods are really practical if you want the motor to last past 30k miles.  A HO cam (w/ steel gears) couldn't hurt.  Headers and a Holley intake/TBI would nice too.  But, I think the best way to spend your money would be to replace the Duke with a Quad4 or V6.  Hope this helps.<BR>Scott   ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Fatal Error||08-03-2001||03:35 AM||||Thanks guys!<P>I'm thinking that it might be more worth while to go ahead and upgrade to a V6 .. most likely a 3.4L. I also did a search of previous posts and found a metric a$$ load of info. Thanks again for all the info!!!<P>-Fatal||||reg||10
